#: ../../../cmake-modules/PythonExtensions.rst:2
msgid "PythonExtensions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:3
msgid ""
"This module defines CMake functions to build Python extension modules and "
"stand-alone executables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:6
msgid "The following variables are defined: ::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:9
msgid ""
"PYTHON_PREFIX                     - absolute path to the current Python\n"
"                                    distribution's prefix\n"
"PYTHON_SITE_PACKAGES_DIR          - absolute path to the current Python\n"
"                                    distribution's site-packages directory\n"
"PYTHON_RELATIVE_SITE_PACKAGES_DIR - path to the current Python\n"
"                                    distribution's site-packages directory\n"
"                                    relative to its prefix\n"
"PYTHON_SEPARATOR                  - separator string for file path\n"
"                                    components.  Equivalent to ``os.sep`` "
"in\n"
"                                    Python.\n"
"PYTHON_PATH_SEPARATOR             - separator string for PATH-style\n"
"                                    environment variables.  Equivalent to\n"
"                                    ``os.pathsep`` in Python.\n"
"PYTHON_EXTENSION_MODULE_SUFFIX    - suffix of the compiled module. For "
"example, on\n"
"                                    Linux, based on environment, it could be "
"``.cpython-35m-x86_64-linux-gnu.so``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:27
#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UsePythonExtensions.cmake:3
msgid "The following functions are defined:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:31
msgid ""
"For libraries meant to be used as Python extension modules, either "
"dynamically loaded or directly linked.  Amend the configuration of the "
"library target (created using ``add_library``) with additional options "
"needed to build and use the referenced library as a Python extension module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:36
msgid "python_extension_module(<Target>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:37
msgid ""
"[LINKED_MODULES_VAR <LinkedModVar>] [FORWARD_DECL_MODULES_VAR "
"<ForwardDeclModVar>] [MODULE_SUFFIX <ModuleSuffix>])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:41
msgid ""
"Only extension modules that are configured to be built as MODULE libraries "
"can be runtime-loaded through the standard Python import mechanism.  All "
"other modules can only be included in standalone applications that are "
"written to expect their presence.  In addition to being linked against the "
"libraries for these modules, such applications must forward declare their "
"entry points and initialize them prior to use.  To generate these forward "
"declarations and initializations, see ``python_modules_header``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:49
msgid ""
"If ``<Target>`` does not refer to a target, then it is assumed to refer to "
"an extension module that is not linked at all, but compiled along with other "
"source files directly into an executable.  Adding these modules does not "
"cause any library configuration modifications, and they are not added to the "
"list of linked modules.  They still must be forward declared and "
"initialized, however, and so are added to the forward declared modules list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:56
msgid ""
"If the associated target is of type ``MODULE_LIBRARY``, the LINK_FLAGS "
"target property is used to set symbol visibility and export only the module "
"init function. This applies to GNU and MSVC compilers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:60
#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:141
msgid "Options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:62
msgid "``LINKED_MODULES_VAR <LinkedModVar>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:63
msgid ""
"Name of the variable referencing a list of extension modules whose libraries "
"must be linked into the executables of any stand-alone applications that use "
"them.  By default, the global property ``PY_LINKED_MODULES_LIST`` is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:67
msgid "``FORWARD_DECL_MODULES_VAR <ForwardDeclModVar>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:68
msgid ""
"Name of the variable referencing a list of extension modules whose entry "
"points must be forward declared and called by any stand-alone applications "
"that use them.  By default, the global property "
"``PY_FORWARD_DECL_MODULES_LIST`` is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:73
msgid "``MODULE_SUFFIX <ModuleSuffix>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:74
msgid ""
"Suffix appended to the python extension module file. The default suffix is "
"retrieved using ``sysconfig.get_config_var(\"EXT_SUFFIX\")``, if not "
"available, the default is then ``.so`` on unix and ``.pyd`` on windows. "
"Setting the variable ``PYTHON_EXTENSION_MODULE_SUFFIX`` in the caller scope "
"defines the value used for all extensions not having a suffix explicitly "
"specified using ``MODULE_SUFFIX`` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:85
msgid "python_standalone_executable(<Target>)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:87
msgid ""
"For standalone executables that initialize their own Python runtime (such as "
"when building source files that include one generated by Cython with the --"
"embed option).  Amend the configuration of the executable target (created "
"using ``add_executable``) with additional options needed to properly build "
"the referenced executable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:96
msgid ""
"Generate a header file that contains the forward declarations and "
"initialization routines for the given list of Python extension modules. "
"``<Name>`` is the logical name for the header file (no file extensions). "
"``<HeaderFilename>`` is the actual destination filename for the header file "
"(e.g.: decl_modules.h)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:102
msgid "python_modules_header(<Name> [HeaderFilename]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:103
msgid ""
"[FORWARD_DECL_MODULES_LIST <ForwardDeclModList>] [HEADER_OUTPUT_VAR "
"<HeaderOutputVar>] [INCLUDE_DIR_OUTPUT_VAR <IncludeDirOutputVar>])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:107
msgid ""
"If only ``<Name>`` is provided, and it ends in the \".h\" extension, then it "
"is assumed to be the ``<HeaderFilename>``.  The filename of the header file "
"without the extension is used as the logical name.  If only ``<Name>`` is "
"provided, and it does not end in the \".h\" extension, then the "
"``<HeaderFilename>`` is assumed to be ``<Name>.h``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:113
msgid ""
"The exact contents of the generated header file depend on the logical "
"``<Name>``.  It should be set to a value that corresponds to the target "
"application, or for the case of multiple applications, some identifier that "
"conveys its purpose.  It is featured in the generated multiple inclusion "
"guard as well as the names of the generated initialization routines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:119
msgid ""
"The generated header file includes forward declarations for all listed "
"modules, as well as implementations for the following class of routines:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:122
msgid "``int <Name>_<Module>(void)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:123
msgid ""
"Initializes the python extension module, ``<Module>``.  Returns an integer "
"handle to the module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:126
msgid "``void <Name>_LoadAllPythonModules(void)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:127
msgid "Initializes all listed python extension modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:129
msgid "``void CMakeLoadAllPythonModules(void);``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:130
msgid ""
"Alias for ``<Name>_LoadAllPythonModules`` whose name does not depend on "
"``<Name>``.  This function is excluded during preprocessing if the "
"preprocessing macro ``EXCLUDE_LOAD_ALL_FUNCTION`` is defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:134
msgid "``void Py_Initialize_Wrapper();``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:135
msgid ""
"Wrapper around ``Py_Initialize()`` that initializes all listed python "
"extension modules.  This function is excluded during preprocessing if the "
"preprocessing macro ``EXCLUDE_PY_INIT_WRAPPER`` is defined.  If this "
"function is generated, then ``Py_Initialize()`` is redefined to a macro that "
"calls this function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:143
msgid "``FORWARD_DECL_MODULES_LIST <ForwardDeclModList>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:144
msgid ""
"List of extension modules for which to generate forward declarations of "
"their entry points and their initializations.  By default, the global "
"property ``PY_FORWARD_DECL_MODULES_LIST`` is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:148
msgid "``HEADER_OUTPUT_VAR <HeaderOutputVar>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:149
msgid ""
"Name of the variable to set to the path to the generated header file.  By "
"default, ``<Name>`` is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:152
msgid "``INCLUDE_DIR_OUTPUT_VAR <IncludeDirOutputVar>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:153
msgid ""
"Name of the variable to set to the path to the directory containing the "
"generated header file.  By default, ``<Name>_INCLUDE_DIRS`` is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:156
msgid "Defined variables:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:158
msgid "``<HeaderOutputVar>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:159
msgid "The path to the generated header file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:161
msgid "``<IncludeDirOutputVar>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:162
msgid "Directory containing the generated header file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:166
#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UsePythonExtensions.cmake:21
#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UsePythonExtensions.cmake:51
msgid "Example usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/FindPythonExtensions.cmake:168
msgid ""
"find_package(PythonExtensions)\n"
"find_package(Cython)\n"
"find_package(Boost COMPONENTS python)\n"
"\n"
"# Simple Cython Module -- no executables\n"
"add_cython_target(_module.pyx)\n"
"add_library(_module MODULE ${_module})\n"
"python_extension_module(_module)\n"
"\n"
"# Mix of Cython-generated code and C++ code using Boost Python\n"
"# Stand-alone executable -- no modules\n"
"include_directories(${Boost_INCLUDE_DIRS})\n"
"add_cython_target(main.pyx CXX EMBED_MAIN)\n"
"add_executable(main boost_python_module.cxx ${main})\n"
"target_link_libraries(main ${Boost_LIBRARIES})\n"
"python_standalone_executable(main)\n"
"\n"
"# stand-alone executable with three extension modules:\n"
"# one statically linked, one dynamically linked, and one loaded at runtime\n"
"#\n"
"# Freely mixes Cython-generated code, code using Boost-Python, and\n"
"# hand-written code using the CPython API.\n"
"\n"
"# module1 -- statically linked\n"
"add_cython_target(module1.pyx)\n"
"add_library(module1 STATIC ${module1})\n"
"python_extension_module(module1\n"
"                        LINKED_MODULES_VAR linked_module_list\n"
"                        FORWARD_DECL_MODULES_VAR fdecl_module_list)\n"
"\n"
"# module2 -- dynamically linked\n"
"include_directories(${Boost_INCLUDE_DIRS})\n"
"add_library(module2 SHARED boost_module2.cxx)\n"
"target_link_libraries(module2 ${Boost_LIBRARIES})\n"
"python_extension_module(module2\n"
"                        LINKED_MODULES_VAR linked_module_list\n"
"                        FORWARD_DECL_MODULES_VAR fdecl_module_list)\n"
"\n"
"# module3 -- loaded at runtime\n"
"add_cython_target(module3a.pyx)\n"
"add_library(module3 MODULE ${module3a} module3b.cxx)\n"
"target_link_libraries(module3 ${Boost_LIBRARIES})\n"
"python_extension_module(module3\n"
"                        LINKED_MODULES_VAR linked_module_list\n"
"                        FORWARD_DECL_MODULES_VAR fdecl_module_list)\n"
"\n"
"# application executable -- generated header file + other source files\n"
"python_modules_header(modules\n"
"                      FORWARD_DECL_MODULES_LIST ${fdecl_module_list})\n"
"include_directories(${modules_INCLUDE_DIRS})\n"
"\n"
"add_cython_target(mainA)\n"
"add_cython_target(mainC)\n"
"add_executable(main ${mainA} mainB.cxx ${mainC} mainD.c)\n"
"\n"
"target_link_libraries(main ${linked_module_list} ${Boost_LIBRARIES})\n"
"python_standalone_executable(main)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UsePythonExtensions.cmake:7
msgid ""
"Add a library that contains a mix of C, C++, Fortran, Cython, F2PY, "
"Template, and Tempita sources. The required targets are automatically "
"generated to \"lower\" source files from their high-level representation to "
"a file that the compiler can accept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UsePythonExtensions.cmake:13
msgid "add_python_library(<Name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UsePythonExtensions.cmake:14
#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UsePythonExtensions.cmake:44
msgid ""
"SOURCES [source1 [source2 ...]] [INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES [dir1 [dir2 ...]] "
"[LINK_LIBRARIES [lib1 [lib2 ...]] [DEPENDS [source1 [source2 ...]]])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UsePythonExtensions.cmake:23
msgid ""
"find_package(PythonExtensions)\n"
"\n"
"file(GLOB arpack_sources ARPACK/SRC/*.f ARPACK/UTIL/*.f)\n"
"\n"
" add_python_library(arpack_scipy\n"
"   SOURCES ${arpack_sources}\n"
"           ${g77_wrapper_sources}\n"
"   INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES ARPACK/SRC\n"
" )"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UsePythonExtensions.cmake:37
msgid ""
"Add a extension that contains a mix of C, C++, Fortran, Cython, F2PY, "
"Template, and Tempita sources. The required targets are automatically "
"generated to \"lower\" source files from their high-level representation to "
"a file that the compiler can accept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UsePythonExtensions.cmake:43
msgid "add_python_extension(<Name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../skbuild/resources/cmake/UsePythonExtensions.cmake:53
msgid ""
"find_package(PythonExtensions)\n"
"\n"
"file(GLOB arpack_sources ARPACK/SRC/*.f ARPACK/UTIL/*.f)\n"
"\n"
" add_python_extension(arpack_scipy\n"
"   SOURCES ${arpack_sources}\n"
"           ${g77_wrapper_sources}\n"
"   INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES ARPACK/SRC\n"
" )"
msgstr ""
